        "original_id": "8a95a938-57ce-5b8c-bceb-29f2ca9146a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cressida Cowell, Neal Layton\n- Companies: DreamWorks Animation\n- Products: How to Train Your Dragon franchise, Legend of the Boneknapper Dragon, Book of Dragons, Gift of the Night Fury, Dawn of the Dragon Racers, That Rabbit Belongs to Emily Brown\n- Topics: short films, children's books, screen adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Cressida Cowell was born on 15 April 1966 and is an English children's author.\n- That Rabbit Belongs to Emily Brown is a children's picture book written by Cressida Cowell, illustrated by Neal Layton, and published in 2006.\n- Legend of the Boneknapper Dragon is a 2010 animated short film by DreamWorks Animation and a sequel to the feature film How to Train Your Dragon.\n- Book of Dragons and Gift of the Night Fury were released in 2011 as short films in the How to Train Your Dragon franchise.\n- Dawn of the Dragon Racers was released in 2014 as a short film in the How to Train Your Dragon franchise.\n- Cressida Cowell is popularly known for the novel series How to Train Your Dragon, which DreamWorks Animation adapted into an award-winning screen franchise.\n- The How to Train Your Dragon franchise also consists of four short films: Legend of the Boneknapper Dragon, Book of Dragons, Gift of the Night Fury, and Dawn of the Dragon Racers.",
